Renting a château for a weekend means gathering everyone you love under one roof, with no compromises and no neighbours. Not just another holiday cottage, not a hotel where everyone shuts themselves away in their room: a large family home that you have entirely to yourselves. At the Château de la Huberdière, in Touraine near Amboise, you have a fourteen-hectare estate and 21 beds at your disposal, 2 hrs 20 from Paris.

Family reunion, get-together with friends, birthday or a weekend of celebration: here is how a large-capacity château hire unfolds, and why this format changes everything.

## Rent a château for a group, not a room

Most group accommodation simply houses you, nothing more. A privately hired château does the opposite: it gives you the whole place. The château's 10 bedrooms, each with its own bathroom, sleep up to 21 people. The grounds, the pool, the sitting rooms, the big table: it is all yours, with no set timetables and no communal areas shared with strangers.

That is what people are after when they want to rent a château with friends or family: a place where the group lives at its own pace. You meet in the early morning around the coffee, the children run in the grounds, the adults carry the evening on without disturbing anyone.

## A large-capacity estate

La Huberdière matches the intention of anyone looking for a holiday cottage for 20 people, with the added soul of a real château.

- 10 characterful rooms and suites, sleeps 21, private bathroom
- Four sitting rooms for a grand dinner for up to 22 guests
- A kitchen at your disposal to prepare your meals
- Fourteen hectares of walled grounds and a pool heated from April to October

There is no shortage of space, inside or out. You can bring everyone together for a big meal, then scatter across the sitting rooms, the grounds or by the pool. Everyone finds their corner, the group keeps its unity.

## A weekend with friends or a family reunion

The most common format is still the weekend, from Friday to Sunday. Two nights are enough to switch off, to properly reconnect, without the fatigue of a long journey. The château suits a cousins' gathering just as well as a milestone birthday, a low-key stag or hen weekend, or simply a reunion of old friends.

We leave you free to live the place your way. You cook for yourselves or you hand the meals to us; you organise your own activities or you ask us for advice. Our role is to make the logistics invisible so you can enjoy your own people.

## What to do during your stay

The estate is enough on its own, but Touraine is right there. From the château, you range out without ever driving far.

- A swim in the heated pool, a game of pétanque or table tennis in the grounds
- An Italian cookery class with me, drawn from my roots and the market
- A wine tasting in Vouvray or Montlouis-sur-Loire, a few minutes away
- A château day: Amboise and the Clos Lucé ten minutes away, Chenonceau twenty

To plan the visits, our guide to [visiting the Loire Valley châteaux](/en/blog/visiter-chateaux-de-la-loire) gives a first itinerary. And if some of you want to stay on, the [stay at the château](/en/sejour) page details the rooms and their rates.

## Book the château hire

For a weekend, a long weekend or a week, exclusive hire of the château can be booked all year round. The details of the spaces, the capacity and the package are on the [family reunion and château hire](/en/famille) page.

Tell us your dates, the number of guests and the spirit of your stay. We send you a tailored proposal within 24 hours, and we prepare the château so all you have to do is arrive.
